  "prefLabel": "Env-A 2704.01 Fugitive Dust Control Within Plant Property",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 2704.01 Fugitive Dust Control Within Plant Property.\n\n(a) The owner or operator of a hot mix asphalt plant shall control the emission of dust caused by vehicular movement within the plant property boundaries using methods that include, but are not limited to, paving or wetting the roadway.\n\n(b) The owner or operator of a hot mix asphalt plant shall control emissions of dust from ancillary devices and sources, such as overflow chutes, aggregate cold feed bins, feeders, aggregate conveyors, and stockpiles, using methods that include, but are not limited to, wet suppression, windbreaks, enclosures, or soil stabilization.\n\nSource. #6428-B, eff 1-18-97 (formerly Env-A 1209); ss by #8217, eff 11-24-04; ss by #10272, eff 2-16-13 (formerly Env-A 2705.01); ss by #13492, eff 11-19-22\n\nAppendix",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a2700.html"
